{%- assign pg_gift_p = all_products['r36s-protective-case-free-gift'] -%}
{%- assign pg_gift_v = pg_gift_p.variants | first -%}
{%- assign pg_gift_was = pg_gift_v.compare_at_price | money -%}
{%- if pg_gift_v.compare_at_price == nil or pg_gift_v.compare_at_price == 0 -%}{%- assign pg_gift_was = '$13.99' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  PG Cart Tune: the drawer's small corrections.

  NO "YOU SAVED (57%)" ROW. pg-cart-total renders the summary block as
  Subtotal / Extra 10% Off / You saved (n%), and the theme's own Total sits
  right beneath it. Per the owner the saved line comes out: the discount rows
  above it already say what came off, and repeating it as a percentage next to
  the real total is noise at the moment of paying. Only that row is hidden —
  Subtotal and Extra 10% Off stay, and pg-cart-total keeps computing the block,
  so nothing downstream of it changes.

  SHIPPING PROTECTION, BIGGER. In the sticky panel pg-drawer shrinks the whole
  box hard -- icon 42px to 28px and its svg 22 to 16, title 14.5 to 12.5px, sub
  12 to 10.5px, price 14.5 to 12.5px -- and it reads as fine print beside the
  checkout button. All five are stepped back up, the words, the icon and the
  price together. The padding stays trimmed and the sub-line's leading with it,
  because the panel is sticky and height added there pushes checkout down.

  THE UPSELL ROW STOPS EATING THE DRAWER. nc-cro's recommendation rows put the
  product name on as many lines as it wants and drop the SAVE % chip onto a line
  of its own, so one upsell ran several lines deep in a drawer that has to show
  the cart as well. The name is now one line with an ellipsis, and the chip sits
  beside the price where it belongs. The row's own padding is trimmed a couple of
  pixels with it.

  AND THE CHIP STOPS WRAPPING. The first attempt at "beside the price" set
  `#cart .nc-rec-price{display:inline-block}`, on the assumption that the chip was
  a SIBLING of the price. It is not: reading nc-cro, .nc-rec-price is the flex ROW
  that contains the price, the struck was-price and .nc-rec-off together
  (`.nc-rec-off{align-self:center !important;flex:0 0 auto !important}`). Setting
  it inline-block destroyed the flex context, so its children became inline-level
  and broke across lines like words -- the SAVE % on a row of its own. It is a
  flex row again here, with flex-wrap:nowrap, which nc-cro sets early and then
  overrides to wrap later in the same file.

  The title's element is not the same on every row (the markup comes from
  nc-cro), so the nowrap rule lists the candidates it can be rather than
  guessing one — anything not present simply matches nothing.

  THE TOP OF THE DRAWER: THE WHITE BAND AND THE FAINT RULES. Three things stack
  above the first cart line, and two of them are hairlines the owner could see
  and not name. Read off the sections that draw them:

    - pg-drawer's .pg-cart-top is the sticky "Your Cart" header, and it carries
      `border-bottom:1px solid rgba(122,47,162,.16)` -- a faint PURPLE rule;
    - nc-cartfix's .nc-drawer-top is the logo + "Free shipping on every order"
      block, `padding:2px 0 14px`, `margin:0 0 8px`, and its own
      `border-bottom:1px solid rgba(15,42,51,.08)` sitting directly under that
      pill -- the second rule, and the band of empty white between them.

  Both borders come off and the block is compressed: 14px of bottom pad to 6px,
  8px of margin to 4px, and the logo's own 12px bottom margin to 7px. Roughly
  25px comes back at the top of the drawer with nothing removed from it. The
  upsell block's heading and note are trimmed with them, being the next tallest
  thing above the cart itself. .pg-bar's border stays: that one outlines the
  free-shipping progress card, so it reads as a box rather than a stray line.

  THE FREE GIFT LINE'S SAVE %, AND WHY NO RULE COULD PRODUCE ONE. The gift line
  never had a percentage and never could:

    - pg-drawer's pgDeals, which builds .pg-save-chip, returns early on any row
      whose link contains 'free-gift', so no chip is ever created on that line;
    - pg-drawer then hides .pg-save-chip on it as well, so un-hiding an element
      that does not exist changes nothing (that rule is dropped here);
    - pg-chips DOES reach the row, but writes the word FREE into a chip it finds
      rather than creating one.

  So a chip of its own is added: .pg-gift-off, reading -100% to match the -n% the
  other rows carry. Its own class is the point -- nothing else in the theme
  writes it, so there is no second writer to race, and the ping-pong that made
  the add-on label flicker cannot repeat here. It is mounted only when it is
  missing or not already last in its host, so a settled line is left untouched.

  THE FREE GIFT LINE READS LIKE THE OTHERS. By request: struck old price, $0.00,
  and the percentage stacked under them in the bottom-right corner. That corner
  is .nc-lsave -- pg-drawer gives it `grid-area:pr`, `flex-direction:column`,
  `align-items:flex-end`, and styles .nc-lsave-was (grey, struck) and
  .nc-lsave-now (purple, 800, 18px) inside it. So rather than invent a cell, the
  gift line is given one built from those same class names, and it inherits the
  format every other line already uses.

  It is only built when the line has no .nc-lsave of its own, and torn down again
  the moment a real one appears, so there is never a second price cell. pg-chips'
  repct() then keeps the figures honest by itself: it treats the $0.00 line as a
  free row and writes money(0) into .nc-lsave-now and compare-at x qty into the
  struck element -- the same values, so there is nothing to race over.

  The struck figure's default comes from Liquid (`all_products[...]`), not a
  constant in the script, so it follows the variant's compare-at if it is ever
  repriced.

  THE WORDS INSIDE THE FREE GIFT PILL, LEFT. pg-drawer's ftFix() measures where
  the glyphs actually paint and pulls them over with a negative `text-indent`,
  writing it INLINE and !important -- unbeatable from a stylesheet, which is why
  the padding rule below never moved them. When that measurement is taken before
  the webfont settles the correction lands the wrong way and the words sit right
  of centre. ftFix runs at creation and again at 400/1500/3500ms and on
  fonts.ready, and then stops -- it is not on an interval. So the indent is
  zeroed here only once a pill is older than four seconds, which is after ftFix's
  last scheduled run: no two writers alternating, no flicker while the font
  loads, and the correction sticks because nothing writes it again.

  THE SPARE CASE LINE, SLIGHTLY BIGGER. Its title is stepped up from the drawer's
  16.5px/700 to 17.5px/800. Scoped to the case product's own rows and excluding
  the gift line, which is deliberately the thinner module.

  THE FREE GIFT PILL, LEFT. It is pulled to the left edge of its line, under
  the product title. pg-drawer's ftFix() writes an inline text-indent and width
  on it from a measurement taken before the webfont settles, and inline
  !important cannot be beaten from a stylesheet — but with the pill's own box
  restated here it lands correctly as soon as ftFix is not fighting it.

  WHY pg-gift-fix IS GONE. It added the free case itself. So does pg-giftguard,
  which already owned that job — pg-drawer's own giftSync was disabled in favour
  of it, with a comment saying exactly why: "re-enabling this add would mean TWO
  owners racing to add the same gift and a cart that intermittently holds two of
  them. One owner." pg-gift-fix made a third owner, on its own clock, each
  refreshing the drawer after its own add. That is the cart glitching, and the
  second case. Deleted, not patched — the gift needs one owner and it already
  has one.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  /* the saved-percent row in the drawer's total block */
  #cart .pg-tot-r.pg-tot-saved,
  body.template-cart .pg-tot-r.pg-tot-saved{display:none !important}

  /* SHIPPING PROTECTION, BIGGER — WORDS, ICON AND PRICE. pg-drawer shrinks the
     whole box hard inside the sticky panel (icon 42px → 28px, its svg 22 → 16,
     title 14.5 → 12.5px, sub 12 → 10.5px, price 14.5 → 12.5px) and it reads as
     fine print beside the checkout button. Every one of those five is stepped
     back up here. The panel is sticky, so the padding stays trimmed and the
     sub-line's leading is tightened — the type grows, the box barely does. */
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp{padding:8px 11px !important;gap:11px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-ic{width:36px !important;height:36px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-ic svg{width:21px !important;height:21px !important;stroke-width:2 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-t b{font-size:15px !important;line-height:1.2 !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-t small{font-size:12.5px !important;line-height:1.2 !important;margin-top:1px !important}
  #cart .sticky-in-panel .pg-sp-price{font-size:15.5px !important;font-weight:800 !important}
  /* outside the sticky panel (cart page, drawer body) it starts roomier, so it
     takes the same step from a higher base */
  #cart .pg-sp-ic{width:46px;height:46px}
  #cart .pg-sp-ic svg{width:25px;height:25px;stroke-width:2}
  #cart .pg-sp-t b{font-size:16px}
  #cart .pg-sp-t small{font-size:13px;line-height:1.3}
  #cart .pg-sp-price{font-size:16px;font-weight:800}

  /* the in-cart upsell rows: one-line name, chip beside the price, less height */
  #cart .nc-rec{padding-top:7px !important;padding-bottom:7px !important}
  #cart .nc-rec-info{min-width:0 !important}
  #cart .nc-rec-info > h3,
  #cart .nc-rec-info > h4,
  #cart .nc-rec-info > b,
  #cart .nc-rec-info > a,
  #cart .nc-rec-info > .nc-rec-t,
  #cart .nc-rec-info > .nc-rec-title,
  #cart .nc-rec-t,
  #cart .nc-rec-title{
    display:block !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
    overflow:hidden !important;
    text-overflow:ellipsis !important;
    max-width:100% !important;
  }
  /* THE PRICE ROW IS A FLEX CONTAINER, AND IT MUST STAY ONE. .nc-rec-price is
     not a sibling of the SAVE chip -- it is the row that HOLDS it, along with
     the struck was-price (nc-cro: `.nc-rec-off{align-self:center;flex:0 0 auto}`).
     The previous pass here set `#cart .nc-rec-price{display:inline-block}` to put
     the chip beside the price, which instead blockified the flex context: its
     children became inline-level and broke across lines like words, which is the
     SAVE % dropping onto a second row.

     nc-cro itself sets `flex-wrap:nowrap` on this element early in the file and
     then `flex-wrap:wrap !important` later, so the later rule wins and the row
     was free to break in any case. Both are plain class selectors, so #cart here
     outranks them on specificity regardless of order. */
  #cart .nc-rec-price{
    display:flex !important;align-items:center !important;
    flex-wrap:nowrap !important;row-gap:0 !important;gap:5px !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;min-width:0 !important;
  }
  #cart .nc-rec-price > *{flex:0 0 auto !important;white-space:nowrap !important}
  #cart .nc-rec-was{white-space:nowrap !important}
  #cart .nc-rec-off{
    white-space:nowrap !important;flex:0 0 auto !important;
    margin-left:3px !important;padding:2px 8px !important;line-height:1.4 !important;
  }

  /* no hairline above or below the free-shipping pill, and less air with it;
     the upsell block's heading + note are the next tallest thing above the cart */
  #cart .nc-drawer-top{padding:0 0 6px !important;margin:0 0 4px !important;border-bottom:0 !important}
  #cart .nc-dlogo,#cart .nc-dlogo-txt{margin-bottom:7px !important}
  #cart .pg-cart-top{border-bottom:0 !important;padding-top:9px !important;padding-bottom:9px !important}
  #cart .cart-upsell h3{font-size:14px !important;margin:0 0 2px !important}
  #cart .nc-upsell-note{font-size:11px !important;padding:4px 10px !important;margin:2px 0 7px !important}
  #cart .nc-recs,
  #cart .nc-recs-panel{margin-top:2px !important}

  /* the FREE GIFT pill sits at the left edge of its line, under the title */
  #cart .pg-free-tag,
  body.template-cart .pg-free-tag{
    width:max-content !important;
    text-indent:0 !important;
    padding:6px 12px !important;
    text-align:left !important;
    justify-self:start !important;
    align-self:start !important;
    margin-left:0 !important;
    margin-right:auto !important;
  }
  /* and the gift line gets its own percentage, in the price corner under the
     struck $13.99 and the $0.00 -- geometry and colour matched to .pg-save-chip
     so the two read as the same badge on different rows */
  #cart .pg-gift-off,
  body.template-cart .pg-gift-off{
    display:inline-flex !important;align-items:center !important;justify-content:center !important;
    background-image:linear-gradient(120deg,#9B4BC4 0%,#7A2FA2 30%,#4A1C66 50%,#7A2FA2 70%,#9B4BC4 100%);
    background-size:240% 240%;animation:pgShift 5s ease-in-out infinite;
    color:#fff !important;-webkit-text-fill-color:#fff !important;
    font-size:12px !important;font-weight:700 !important;line-height:1 !important;
    letter-spacing:normal !important;word-spacing:normal !important;text-indent:0 !important;
    padding:6px 7px !important;border-radius:999px !important;
    width:fit-content !important;max-width:100% !important;min-width:0 !important;flex:none !important;
    margin:2px 0 0 !important;
  }

  /* the spare (paid) case line: a little bigger and bolder than the drawer's
     default. The gift line is excluded -- it is the thinner module on purpose */
  #cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="free-gift"]):not([data-pg-free]) section h2,
  #cart .l4ca > li:has(a[href*="free-gift"]):not([data-pg-free]) section h2 a{
    font-size:17.5px !important;font-weight:800 !important;line-height:1.28 !important;
  }

  /* --- the upsell row on the two phones that matter ---
     iPhone 13/14/16/17 report a 390-393px viewport, the Pro Max models 430-440.
     The row has to fit picture + one-line name + price + chip + ADD in both, so
     the small class steps everything down a point and shrinks the thumbnail,
     and the large class takes the middle size rather than the desktop one. */
  @media (max-width:400px){
    #cart .nc-rec{gap:8px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec img{width:52px !important;height:52px !important;flex:0 0 52px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-t,
    #cart .nc-rec-title{font-size:13px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-price{font-size:13.5px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-was{font-size:11.5px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-price{gap:4px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-off{font-size:10.5px !important;margin-left:2px !important;padding:2px 6px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-add{padding:7px 12px !important;font-size:11.5px !important}
  }
  @media (min-width:401px) and (max-width:480px){
    #cart .nc-rec img{width:58px !important;height:58px !important;flex:0 0 58px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-t,
    #cart .nc-rec-title{font-size:13.5px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-price{font-size:14px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-was{font-size:12px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-off{font-size:11px !important;margin-left:3px !important}
    #cart .nc-rec-add{padding:8px 14px !important;font-size:12px !important}
  }
</style>
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgGiftOff) return; window.pgGiftOff = 1;

  function giftRows(){
    var out = [];
    document.querySelectorAll('#cart .l4ca > li, body.template-cart .form-cart .l4ca > li')
      .forEach(function(li){ if (li.querySelector('.pg-free-tag')) out.push(li); });
    return out;
  }

  var WAS = {{ pg_gift_was | json }};

  /* THE PRICE CELL. .nc-lsave is the bottom-right corner every other line uses;
     if the gift line has one, the chip simply joins it. If it has none, one is
     built from the same class names so pg-drawer's existing rules lay it out and
     colour it -- and it is removed again the moment a real one turns up, so the
     line never carries two. */
  function cellOf(li){
    var real = null, mine = null;
    li.querySelectorAll('.nc-lsave').forEach(function(el){
      if (el.hasAttribute('data-pg-gift-cell')) mine = el; else real = el;
    });
    if (real){
      if (mine && mine.parentNode) mine.parentNode.removeChild(mine);
      return real;
    }
    if (mine) return mine;
    var sect = li.querySelector('section');
    if (!sect) return null;
    var cell = document.createElement('div');
    cell.className = 'nc-lsave';
    cell.setAttribute('data-pg-gift-cell', '1');
    cell.innerHTML = '<s class="nc-lsave-was"></s><b class="nc-lsave-now"></b>';
    cell.querySelector('.nc-lsave-was').textContent = WAS;
    cell.querySelector('.nc-lsave-now').textContent = '$0.00';
    sect.appendChild(cell);
    return cell;
  }

  /* THE WORDS INSIDE THE PILL. Only after ftFix has stopped writing -- see the
     note above. Age is stamped the first time a pill is seen. */
  function pillLeft(li){
    var tag = li.querySelector('.pg-free-tag');
    if (!tag) return;
    var t0 = parseInt(tag.getAttribute('data-pg-seen') || '0', 10);
    if (!t0){ tag.setAttribute('data-pg-seen', String(Date.now())); return; }
    if (Date.now() - t0 < 4000) return;
    if (tag.style.textIndent !== '0px') tag.style.setProperty('text-indent', '0', 'important');
    if (tag.style.width !== 'fit-content') tag.style.setProperty('width', 'fit-content', 'important');
    if (tag.style.textAlign !== 'left') tag.style.setProperty('text-align', 'left', 'important');
    if (tag.style.justifyContent !== 'flex-start') tag.style.setProperty('justify-content', 'flex-start', 'important');
  }

  function pass(){
    giftRows().forEach(function(li){
      pillLeft(li);
      var host = cellOf(li);
      if (!host) return;
      var chip = li.querySelector('.pg-gift-off');
      if (!chip){
        chip = document.createElement('span');
        chip.className = 'pg-gift-off';
        chip.textContent = '-100%';
      }
      /* settle, do not fight: a chip already sitting last in its host is left
         alone, so this writes nothing on the passes after the first */
      if (chip.parentNode !== host || chip !== host.lastElementChild) host.appendChild(chip);
    });
  }

  var pending = false;
  function soon(){
    if (pending) return;
    pending = true;
    setTimeout(function(){ pending = false; pass(); }, 80);
  }

  if (window.MutationObserver){
    (function watch(){
      var c = document.getElementById('cart');
      if (c){ try { new MutationObserver(soon).observe(c, {childList:true, subtree:true}); } catch(e){} }
      else setTimeout(watch, 500);
    })();
  }
  setInterval(pass, 1200);
  pass();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Cart Tune", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG Cart Tune"}]}
{% endschema %}
